          "urpx:selfContained": true,
          "urpx:explainedBy": {
            "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
            "@id": "cpau:cc-e-eec-1-2025-09-01-evaluation",
            "urpx:evaluationKind": {
              "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
            },
            "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. One part is deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Section A bars concurrent time-of-use service (\"This Rate Schedule may not apply in conjunction with any time-of-use Rate Schedule\"). The model carries this only as urpx:description prose; its two EligibilityRules hold three ComparisonNodes (Customer-Generator, a notEqualsOperator NEM test, bidirectional meter) and no time-of-use predicate. The NEM test in the same file shows the exclusion shape is expressible.",
